# Unity-generated, machine/editor-local — none of this should ever be
# committed. Based on Unity's own recommended .gitignore, trimmed to what's
# actually relevant to a solo project (see TagSim3D/README.md for what *does*
# get committed once the project exists: Assets/, ProjectSettings/,
# Packages/manifest.json).

[Ll]ibrary/
[Tt]emp/
[Oo]bj/
[Bb]uild/
[Bb]uilds/
[Ll]ogs/
[Uu]ser[Ss]ettings/
[Mm]emoryCaptures/
[Rr]ecordings/

# Generated per-IDE project/solution files — regenerated by the Editor
# ("Open C# Project") and shouldn't be tracked; commit ProjectSettings/ and
# Packages/manifest.json instead, which is what actually defines the project.
.vs/
.vsconfig
*.csproj
*.unityproj
*.sln
*.suo
*.user
*.userprefs
*.pidb
*.booproj
*.svd
*.pdb
*.mdb
*.opendb
*.VC.db

# Unity crash/diagnostics
sysinfo.txt
*.stackdump

# Asset meta files can go stale/conflict if editors on different platforms
# fight over them — not ignored (they're load-bearing, see README) but noted
# here as the thing to never hand-edit or delete casually.

# Builds
*.apk
*.aab
*.unitypackage
*.app

# OS cruft
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
